{"content":[{"id":"tpl-intent-h","type":"heading","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","level":2,"isToggleable":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intent","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"8038bde9","type":"paragraph","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A simple school registry: the school keeps a registry of its classes, and each class keeps a registry of its students. Students live in one shared registry so a student can belong to more than one class. This serves school administrators who set up the school, its classes and student rosters and keep them current. The registry serves a single school — the School record describes the deployment's one school. [ASSUMED: one school per deployment, from the request's singular \"school entity\"]","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"tpl-scope-h","type":"heading","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","level":2,"isToggleable":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"ede75d2d","type":"bulletListItem","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"IN: the School, Class and Student records; class membership (a class's list of students); uniqueness of class names within a school and of student numbers.","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"77a1f77d","type":"bulletListItem","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"OUT: attendance, grades, timetabling, fees, teachers as managed records (a class's teacher is a free-text name), any lifecycle (archive/withdraw) — records are simply created, edited and deleted.","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"tpl-scenarios-h","type":"heading","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","level":2,"isToggleable":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scenarios ","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"35854427","type":"paragraph","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"None — the beans' standard screens cover create/edit/browse; no journey has an order of steps the screens do not already give.","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"tpl-requirements-h","type":"heading","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","level":2,"isToggleable":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Requirements","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"c1bdd31e","type":"paragraph","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"R1: WHEN a class is created, renamed, or moved to a different school, the system SHALL reject the save when the resulting name already belongs to another class of the same school.","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"tpl-datamodel-h","type":"heading","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","level":2,"isToggleable":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Data model","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"44443eb9","type":"paragraph","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A ","styles":{}},{"type":"text","text":"student","styles":{"bold":true}},{"type":"text","text":" is a person enrolled at a school; a ","styles":{}},{"type":"text","text":"class","styles":{"bold":true}},{"type":"text","text":" is a teaching group within one school; a class's ","styles":{}},{"type":"text","text":"roster","styles":{"bold":true}},{"type":"text","text":" is the students belonging to it. A student may belong to several classes.","styles":{}}],"children":[]},{"id":"0e9820bc","type":"heading","props":{"backgroundColor":"default","textColor":"default","textAlignment":"left","level":3,"isToggleable":fal